+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `npm start` to serve the site and `npm test` to run the timing unit tests.
+
+## Contentful update measurements
+
+`paint-timing.mjs` observes browser-reported `interaction-contentful-paint` and
+`soft-navigation` entries. Each API is feature-detected; unsupported measurements
+are skipped without substituting click-to-next-frame estimates.
+
+The page exposes `window.dailyGrindPerformance`:
+
+```js
+dailyGrindPerformance.support;      // Supported measurements in this browser
+dailyGrindPerformance.getReports(); // Last 100 reports, oldest first
+dailyGrindPerformance.flush();      // Finalize the active route measurement
+dailyGrindPerformance.stop();       // Flush, disconnect, and remove listeners
+
+window.addEventListener('daily-grind:paint-timing', ({ detail }) => {
+  console.log(detail); // Or pass to your own analytics integration
+});
+```
+
+`interaction-paint` reports contain `duration` in milliseconds from the initiating
+input to on-screen presentation. A single interaction can emit several reports as
+larger content is painted. These are contentful paint candidates, not INP scores.
+
+`soft-navigation` reports contain `fcpDuration` and `lcpDuration` measured from
+the initiating input. Reports finalize on the next soft navigation, page hiding,
+page exit, explicit flush, or stop. No LCP candidate is represented by `null`.
+The initial candidate includes content painted before the URL update; subsequent
+candidates are matched by `interactionId`, even if their `navigationId` differs.
+Reports include element tag, ID, and size without retaining DOM references.
+
+The existing links perform full document navigations. They do not produce soft
+navigation metrics; the observer will capture client-side navigations if a router
+is added. No router, simulated timings, analytics endpoint, or UI changes are added.
+Reports stay in memory unless an event consumer explicitly sends them elsewhere.
+
+API reference: [Chrome's soft navigation measurement guide](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/web-platform/soft-navigations).
